{"id": "9-786", "question": "Seasons are caused by what rotating on its axis?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): Our Planet", "B): The Atmosphere", "C): The Equator", "D): The Sun"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "- Seasons are changes in the weather and temperature patterns that occur at different times of the year.\n- These changes are primarily caused by the tilt of Earth's axis relative to its orbit around the Sun.\n- The tilt of the axis means that, as Earth orbits the Sun, different parts of the planet receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year.\n- The Sun's position in the sky changes due to this tilt, resulting in the seasons.\n- The Sun itself does not rotate on its axis; it is the Earth that rotates on its axis.", "initial_cot_probs": [0.5518954396247864, 0.0, 0.0, 0.4481045603752136], "initial_probs": [0.17662841081619263, 0.10713054984807968, 0.011291475966572762, 0.6985788941383362], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 0, "rt_lambda": 1.0, "word_type_group": "modifier", "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "D): The Sun. The Sun's tilt on", "probs": [0.17662841081619263, 0.10713054984807968, 0.011291475966572762, 0.6985788941383362], "prediction": 3, "target_cot_step": "- Seasons are changes in the weather and temperature patterns that occur at different times of the year.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: Seasons are caused by what rotating on its axis?\n\nChoices:\n(A): Our Planet\n(B): The Atmosphere\n(C): The Equator\n(D): The Sun\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n", "specificity_preds": [2, 2, 0, 2, 3, 0, 1, 3, 2, 1, 3, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 3, 3], "specificity_probs": [[0.006505713332444429, 0.012154272757470608, 0.9655334949493408, 0.010726109147071838], [0.0440019927918911, 0.0183427594602108, 0.7799538969993591, 0.15358202159404755], [0.9017016291618347, 0.07401617616415024, 0.011350749060511589, 0.0019724643789231777], [0.006216548383235931, 0.05898096784949303, 0.9226176142692566, 0.0054860846139490604], [0.